    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0211" n="199" xml:id="pg199"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation(2)/56: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-23T14:00:00-04:00">June 23, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>248. Department’s telegram No. 120, June 22, 4 p.m. I have just seen Dr. Cantilo
                    and read him the telegram. I stressed most earnestly the importance of his
                    presence at the conference and the real advantages, aside from the gesture, that
                    would be afforded by his later visit to the United States referring to the
                    matters discussed in the Department’s telegrams Nos. 121, June 22, 5 p.m., and
                    122, June 22, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="29" xml:id="d259-f1"/> as evidencing the
                    recognition on the part of our Government of the difficulty of the situation in
                    Argentina and the desire of our Government to do everything possible to be of
                    assistance.</p>
                <p>Dr. Cantilo asked me to tell you that nothing would give him personally greater
                    pleasure than to attend the conference and collaborate with you in the important
                    work ahead of us. He particularly appreciated the invitation to visit the United
                    States later and realized the opportunity personal talks with the President and
                    officials of our Government would offer. He told me President Ortiz has thus far
                    been reluctant for him to leave the country at this critical juncture, but he
                    will take up the matter again in the light of your very generous telegram and
                    hopes to have a reply for me as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
